for $k$ by finding a point on the graph and substituting for $x$ and $y.$ The labeled point on the graph is $(0,6),$ so we substitute $x=0$ and $y=6$ into the function and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =k({4}^{x})+4 \\\\ 6 & =k({4}^{0})+4 \\\\ 6 & =k(1)+4 \\\\ 6 & =k+4 \\\\ 2 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=2$ and $c=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["d42f164a-8f93-5002-9420-b8b8cc5382ea"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "89af3be3-33fe-57cd-8d48-22e372069ed4" :answer/id #uuid "89af3be3-33fe-57cd-8d48-22e372069ed4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=6$ and $c=-4$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e179f548-f04b-5311-8704-f1dc1a212d95" :answer/id #uuid "e179f548-f04b-5311-8704-f1dc1a212d95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=4$ and $c=-2$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7a3de642-7b63-53f5-97c1-01b574a6a457" :answer/id #uuid "7a3de642-7b63-53f5-97c1-01b574a6a457" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=6$ and $c=-3$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dec243e8-ab78-5993-bb10-8a2ec1af4863" :answer/id #uuid "dec243e8-ab78-5993-bb10-8a2ec1af4863" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=5$ and $c=-3$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a4bd573d-4c49-560a-a12f-f9f0a7c91dc6" :answer/id #uuid "a4bd573d-4c49-560a-a12f-f9f0a7c91dc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$k=2$ and $c=-3$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "34ba0a92-dd10-5177-98cc-3c51dda20bd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "34ba0a92-dd10-5177-98cc-3c51dda20bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["89af3be3-33fe-57cd-8d48-22e372069ed4" "e179f548-f04b-5311-8704-f1dc1a212d95" "7a3de642-7b63-53f5-97c1-01b574a6a457" "dec243e8-ab78-5993-bb10-8a2ec1af4863" "a4bd573d-4c49-560a-a12f-f9f0a7c91dc6"] :answer-field/correct "dec243e8-ab78-5993-bb10-8a2ec1af4863" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "233d6bb5-1ddb-5d78-a70c-c0